---
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import './Hero.css';
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="container hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">
        <Icon name="lucide:git-branch" size={14} />
        Open source · AGPL server · Apache agent
      </p>
      <h1>Remote monitoring with a&nbsp;memory.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        OpenRMM manages Windows, macOS, and Linux fleets: telemetry, alerting, a
        real terminal in your browser, scripts, and patching. And it keeps
        device history on two time axes, so it can answer what was true on a
        machine <em>and</em> what you believed at the time.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#quick-start">
          <Icon name="lucide:terminal" size={18} />
          Self-host in minutes
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#time-machine">
          <Icon name="lucide:history" size={18} />
          See the time machine
        </a>
      </div>
      <ul class="hero-facts">
        <li><Icon name="lucide:box" size={15} /> One static agent binary</li>
        <li><Icon name="lucide:shield" size={15} /> Outbound-only, works behind NAT</li>
        <li><Icon name="lucide:bot" size={15} /> MCP server built in</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-term card" role="img" aria-label="Terminal showing an agent enrolling and a fleet status table">
      <div class="term-bar">
        <span class="term-dot"></span><span class="term-dot"></span><span class="term-dot"></span>
        <span class="term-title">openrmm</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="term-body"><code><span class="tl" style="--i:0"><span class="t-prompt">$</span> openrmm-agent install --token ore_5f2…</span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:1"><span class="t-ok">✓</span> enrolled as <span class="t-hl">web-01</span> (linux/amd64)</span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:2"><span class="t-ok">✓</span> service installed: systemd</span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:3"><span class="t-ok">✓</span> connected: wss://rmm.example.com <span class="t-dim">(outbound only)</span></span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:4">&nbsp;</span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:5"><span class="t-prompt">$</span> openrmm fleet status</span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:6"><span class="t-dim">NAME        OS       CPU   MEM   DISK  SEEN</span></span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:7">web-01      linux    12%   38%   61%   <span class="t-ok">now</span></span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:8">mac-studio  macos     4%   52%   47%   <span class="t-ok">2s</span></span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:9">win-lab-3   windows  77%   81%   <span class="t-alert">92%</span>   <span class="t-ok">1s</span>  <span class="t-alert">▲ disk</span></span>
<span class="tl" style="--i:10"><span class="t-prompt">$</span> <span class="t-cursor"></span></span></code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
